# Third-party notices and source-code availability

This release bundles the `aws-tunnel` executable with third-party software. The complete, versioned license texts and notices for the audited release dependency closure are included under `LICENSES/_third-party/`; the directory names identify each Go module path and exact version. For mixed-license modules, every license/notice file in the exact module source tree is preserved at its corresponding relative path. These materials are notices for their respective copyright holders and do not change their license terms. The project license applies only to project-authored material.

The audited Go 1.27.3 compiler/runtime license is `LICENSES/_go/1.27.3/LICENSE`. Its imported distribution-vendored packages are `golang.org/x/crypto` v0.52.1-0.20260526024921-9beb694f9766, `golang.org/x/net` v0.55.1-0.20260731170536-c1d18010be90, and `golang.org/x/text` v0.37.0; their BSD-3-Clause licenses are retained beneath `LICENSES/_go/1.27.3/vendor/` along with the Go toolchain license. These texts and the associated upstream PATENTS files were copied from that exact Go distribution.

## MPL-covered HashiCorp dependency

`github.com/hashicorp/go-version` v1.9.0 is unmodified. Its complete source code form, including its original `LICENSE`, is shipped in `LICENSES/_third-party/github.com__hashicorp__go-version@v1.9.0/source/`. This provides recipients a local, release-attached copy under MPL-2.0. The exact upstream source is also available at https://github.com/hashicorp/go-version/tree/v1.9.0 and the upstream license at https://github.com/hashicorp/go-version/blob/v1.9.0/LICENSE. The source snapshot was obtained from the local Go module cache extracted from Go's module proxy for exact version v1.9.0; its module source files are preserved byte-for-byte, including the original `go.mod`, license, readme and changelog. Source-file SHA-256 values can be independently recomputed from the attached copy. This repository does not claim ownership of HashiCorp source.

## Audit provenance

The dependency inventory was produced with read-only `go list -deps -json ./cmd` for `darwin/amd64`, `darwin/arm64`, `linux/amd64`, and `linux/arm64`, with `CGO_ENABLED=0`, `GOTOOLCHAIN=local`, and `GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly`; the cross-target union is 94 exact module versions (93 modules on each Darwin target, 94 on each Linux target). The release dependency versions are pinned in `go.mod` and `go.sum`. The checked-in texts were copied from those exact-version Go module source trees, including nested license exceptions and full upstream NOTICE files. The compiler and standard-library vendor texts were copied from the Go 1.27.3 distribution; release CI pins this compiler version.

Before changing the runtime dependency set, Go toolchain, or target matrix, rerun the inventory for all release targets, review the resulting license and NOTICE files (including nested licenses), update this bundle, and retain the applicable original texts. Do not replace the attached HashiCorp source snapshot with a URL-only reference.
